  "limitations": [
    "Fifteen held-out fictional records share two task templates and two attack templates with development. This is held-out task-instance evaluation, not an unseen-template/family or representative population benchmark.",
    "One deterministic run per condition; greedy generation does not establish reproducibility across hardware or implementations.",
    "Controls share insertion positions, headers and target labels and differ by only one prompt token, but semantics and wording still differ. Subtraction does not isolate malicious intent from every ordinary contextual difference.",
    "Only three resisted cases, all one attack family. Outcome differences cannot be attributed to resistance/obedience independently of family and task composition.",
    "No intervention, patching, or routing ablation was performed. Distance changes do not establish causal mechanisms or identify responsible experts.",
    "Routing covers all 28 prefill layers; four activation types cover eight selected layers. No full attention patterns or generated-reasoning activations were analyzed.",
    "Layer/token/variant measurements within a task are correlated; task-balanced means do not convert templated records into independent population samples. No significance or generalization claim is made.",
    "Exact-answer scoring cleanly distinguishes the intended outputs here, but it evaluates simple bounded tasks and target-output attacks rather than broader tool-use or real-world harm."
  ],
